    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Bowe Property are delighted to present 7 Gleann Dara to the market, a beautifully maintained three-bedroom semi-detached home ideally positioned in the heart of Ballygarvan Village. Built in 2003 and extending to approximately 100 sq. m., this attractive property offers well-proportioned accommodation together with the added benefit of a rear extension, providing additional living space.The property is ideally situated overlooking a pleasant green area. Internally, the house has been exceptionally well cared for and is presented in excellent condition throughout, with the rear extension providing valuable additional space and enhancing the overall functionality of the home. Located in the heart of Ballygarvan Village, offering a wonderful community atmosphere with a local school, shop, sporting facilities, pubs and convenient transport links, while Cork City, Cork Airport, Carrigaline and Kinsale are all within easy reach. The property also provides excellent access to the South Link Road network, making it particularly convenient for those commuting throughout Cork City and the wider county.\r\n7 Gleann Dara represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a superbly maintained home in a highly sought-after location. With its attractive position overlooking the green, generous accommodation, rear extension and excellent overall condition, this is a home that is sure to appeal to a wide range of buyers."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall:\r\n4.12m x 1.82m \r\nWarm and welcoming entrance, timber floor flows throughout to the kitchen, benefits from built in smart storage units under the stairs. \r\n\r\nLiving Room:\r\n4.95m x 3.30\r\nSpacious living room, benefits from timber floor, bay window and open fire. \r\n\r\nKitchen/ Dining Room:\r\n5.40m  x 3.14m \r\nFully fitted kitchen with both floor and eye level units. Subway backsplash, integrated hob and oven all add to this great space. \r\n\r\nW.C:\r\nLocated off the entrance hall, comprises of two-piece suite. \r\n\r\nFamily Room:\r\n6.02m x 2.31m \r\nLocated off the kitchen, the room benefits from Velux windows, solid fuel stove and direct access to the rear garden. \r\n\r\nLanding\r\nAccess to all bedroom accommodation. \r\n\r\nMaster Bedroom:\r\n3.36m x 2.82m \r\nGenerous double bedroom, overlooking the rear garden. Benefits  \r\nfrom timber floor and built in wardrobes. \r\nEnsuite:  2.45m x 0.66m \r\nThe bathroom comprises a three-piece suite incorporating a shower cubicle fitted with an electric shower. The shower area and floor are fully tiled, providing a practical and easy-to-maintain finish. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2:\r\n3.45m x 2.36m \r\nA spacious double bedroom which has been thoughtfully adapted to suit the current family’s needs. The room is currently divided by a stud partition wall, which can be easily removed if desired, allowing the room to be returned to its original layout and full size. \r\n\r\nBedroom 3:\r\n2.59m x 2.44m \r\nSingle bedroom overlooking the front garden. The room benefits from built in wardrobe. \r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom:\r\n1.80m x 1.71m \r\nFully tiled bathroom comprises of three-piece bath suite with electric shower installed. \r\n\r\nGarden:\r\nTo the front, the property benefits from a neatly laid lawn and private off-street parking. The rear garden offers excellent privacy and features a mature lawn together with a garden shed, providing useful additional storage. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSuperb three bedroom semi detached home\r\nPrivate rear garden with garden shed\r\nOff street parking to the front\r\nConvenient  transport links to Cork city and airport\r\nHighly desirable Ballygarvan location\r\nAll mains services and Gas fired central heating"
      },
      {
